<h1>Variables &amp; types</h1>

<p>
  Bind a value with <code>let</code>. Kex infers the type and the REPL prints
  it after the colon — <code>name</code> is a <code>String</code>,
  <code>count</code> an <code>Int</code>, with no annotations needed.
</p>

<Code code={`let name = "kex"`} replPaste mini />

<Code code={`let count = 42`} replPaste mini />

<p>
  A <code>let</code> can't be reassigned. When you need something that
  changes, reach for <code>var</code> instead and give it a new value:
</p>

<Code code={`var n = 5
n = n + 1
n`} replPaste mini />

<p>
  There's no <code>null</code> in kex. A value that might be missing is an
  <strong>Optional</strong> — written <code>T?</code> — either
  <code>Just(value)</code> or <code>None</code>. <code>.or(default)</code>
  unwraps it, falling back when it's empty.
</p>

<Code code={`Just(5).or(0)`} replPaste mini />

<Code code={`None.or(0)`} replPaste mini />
